---

<section id="agents" class="border-b border-ink-800 py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-sand-50 sm:text-3xl">
          Built to be driven by an agent
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-sand-300">
          A tool that runs inside a pipe has to say what happened without saying it twice. In a pipe
          cargo-q is already quiet: one line per command, no color, and diagnostics only for the
          command that failed. The exit code is the contract — there is nothing to parse.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 text-sm text-sand-300">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-moss-400" aria-hidden="true">●</span>
            <span>
              The exit code is the first failure's own code — <code class="text-sand-100">101</code>
              from <code class="text-sand-100">cargo test</code>, <code class="text-sand-100"
                >130</code
              > on Ctrl-C. Never parse the output to find out.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-moss-400" aria-hidden="true">●</span>
            <span>
              A failure prints one line and the tail of the output. Everything that succeeded is
              discarded.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-moss-400" aria-hidden="true">●</span>
            <span>
              On a terminal, <code class="text-sand-100">--no-fancy</code> drops the overprinting
              status display, so a pseudo-terminal gets the same plain lines.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="text-moss-400" aria-hidden="true">●</span>
            <span>
              <code class="text-sand-100">cargo q -n …</code> first, to see how a command line was
              split before anything is spawned.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="terminal overflow-hidden shadow-2xl shadow-black/40">
        <div class="terminal-bar">in a pipe</div>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-5 text-sm leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-sand-500">$ </span><span class="text-sand-100">cargo q fmt clippy check test</span>

<span class="text-sand-300">[1/4] cargo fmt</span>
<span class="text-sand-300">[2/4] cargo clippy</span>
<span class="text-sand-300">[3/4] cargo check</span>
<span class="text-sand-300">[4/4] cargo test</span>
<span class="text-sand-300">Finished 4 command(s) in 0.23s</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
